\title{Principle of inclusion-exclusion}
\date{2026-04-29T11:11:34Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{What if we have \em{three} (or more) overlapping sets of choices? It is actually possible to come up with a general formula for this situation, known as the \em{Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion}.}

